  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shaikh Israr Ahmad Niyaz Ahmad vs State Of Maharashtra on 13 October, 2022 Author: N.R. Borkar Bench: N.R. Borkar 1-ABA-2835-2022.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2835 Of 2022 Shaikh Israr Ahmad Niyaz Ahmad ... Applicant Versus State of Maharashtra through Wada Police Station, Palghar ... Respondent ......... Mr. Tushar Sonawane for the Applicant. Ms. P.P. Shinde, App for the State. Mr. Santosh Wakchaure, Psi, Wada Police Station, present. ......... Coram : N.R. Borkar, J. Dated : 13 October 2022 P.C. :- . This is an application under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 for anticipatory bail. 2. The applicant is apprehending his arrest in Crime No.265 of 2022 registered at Wada Police Station, Palghar for the offence punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 r/w. 34 of Indian Penal Code and Sections 23, 26(2), 26(2)(iv), 27 and 30(2)(a) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3.",
    "facts": "This is an application under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 for anticipatory bail. 2. The applicant is apprehending his arrest in Crime No.265 of 2022 registered at Wada Police Station, Palghar for the offence punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 r/w. 34 of Indian Penal Code and Sections 23, 26(2), 26(2)(iv), 27 and 30(2)(a) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. On 19th July 2022, the co-accused in the aforesaid crime were found in possession of packets of Gutakha (tobacco products). The allegations against the present Applicant are that the said Gutakha packets were supplied by him. 1-ABA-2835-2022.odt 4.",
    "arguments": "5. The learned Counsel for the applicant submits that except the offence punishable under Section 328 of IPC, all other offences are bailable. It is submitted that the issue of applicability of Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. It is submitted that nothing is to be recovered from the applicant. Shaikh Israr Ahmad Niyaz Ahmad vs State Of Maharashtra on 13 October, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/127032687/ 1 6. On the other hand, the learned APP for the State submits that one of the co-accused in his statement stated that the present applicant has supplied the seized Gutakha packets. It is further submitted that the applicant is involved in five more similar offences and thus the custodial interrogation of the present applicant is necessary.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. The learned Counsel for the applicant submits that except the offence punishable under Section 328 of IPC, all other offences are bailable. It is submitted that the issue of applicability of Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. It is submitted that nothing is to be recovered from the applicant. Shaikh Israr Ahmad Niyaz Ahmad vs State Of Maharashtra on 13 October, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/127032687/ 1 6. On the other hand, the learned APP for the State submits that one of the co-accused in his statement stated that the present applicant has supplied the seized Gutakha packets.",
    "respondent_arguments": "It is further submitted that the applicant is involved in five more similar offences and thus the custodial interrogation of the present applicant is necessary.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
